ignatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c0bafeb721cdb73fbd1c8eb111fad3d57d198e678bb57e62d892c648496231c4","event_uuid":"63ce2d0b-dd43-44a6-b8a0-1147d780c60e","position":{"commit_sha":"9e76cc22aec0fe723ed23768e427244328c13d89","position":"1786704469907363001-63ce2d0b-dd43-44a6-b8a0-1147d780c60e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9fa745aff6a9e465abd78ce668c693ad00d9f5ac305996aeadff73f41b19eb65","event_uuid":"44480b26-a333-4ac3-a7cb-d1c073e8bfc2","position":{"commit_sha":"14977e5bb27d40372331a28a5c77b8f5518e1b8d","position":"1786704656088980001-44480b26-a333-4ac3-a7cb-d1c073e8bfc2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Discovery evidence: a one-unit runtime spy observed four Popen calls in order: one Pandoc invocation and three git rev-parse --show-toplevel invocations on the cold path. Across all 884 production conversions, the same spy counted 1,770 Popen calls total, consistent with 884 Pandoc launches plus 886 repository-root discovery launches after warmup. This ticket intentionally remains open and unclaimed until the active independent-golden remediation lands.","timestamp":1786684090666221001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA confirmed on current origin/main d05bf2bc1be. Dynamic trace: 100 `_convert(\"hello\", pandoc)` calls produced identical `hello` bytes and launched 202 subprocesses: 100 Pandoc plus 102 `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`. `_convert` obtains `communicate(..., timeout=_pandoc_timeout())` at wiki_render.py:393; `_pandoc_timeout` calls `load_config()` at :346; `load_config` invokes `repo_root(root)` before its result-cache lookup at config.py:393; implicit `repo_root` shells out at _config_sources.py:30-53. Resolving `_pandoc_timeout()` once and supplying that constant to the same 100 conversions produced byte-identical results with 103 subprocesses: 100 Pandoc plus 3 one-time root probes. Wall was 3.3395s -> 3.3057s locally (0.0338s saved); the process-count reduction, not this quiet-host timing, is the contention-safe proof. The earlier complete oracle trace observed 884 Pandoc + 886 root-discovery launches. This rules out Pandoc output generation, corpus cardinality, and mutation testing as causes of these extra processes. Defect legitimacy: explicit session contract requires reducing CI work without test-fidelity/behavioral coverage loss; repeated repository discovery is not part of any render assertion and 3/3 maintained OSS examples resolve loop/session-invariant configuration once. Caller sweep found `_render_unit` as the sole production caller and hardening tests as the only direct callers; all depend on timeout value/output behavior, none on the number of config lookups. Expected post-fix behavior is identical bytes/fallback/reaping with config sampled once per render pass and once per standalone direct call. No behavioral dependency blocks repair.","timestamp":1786701098657481001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation pushed as Gerrit change 1773, commit ead96799ce7aaf93d5204e5aea619d996faeb68a. Held-out oracle was RED on origin/main with 3 timeout resolutions for one three-unit render pass, GREEN after the fixer (1 resolution/pass), RED again under the exact defect-seeded mutation (4 = one hoisted + three leaked), and GREEN after restoration. Focused renderer coverage: 90 passed; lint and typecheck passed. Fresh paired 884-unit traces preserved 884 real Pandoc calls and byte-exact outputs: old direct-call shape 29.2378s / 1,770 Popen (884 Pandoc + 886 git-root); repaired explicit-timeout shape 29.0194s / 887 Popen (884 Pandoc + 3 git-root). This eliminates 883 redundant subprocesses but saved only 0.2184s on the quiet local pair, so no critical-path minute claim is made. Verify run 31791259529 is in progress; ticket remains in_progress until LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, submit, and merge.","timestamp":1786702367179756001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final report — merged Gerrit 1773 at ead96799ce.\n\nProblem: 884 real Pandoc conversion assertions also performed 883 redundant repository-root subprocesses.\nProven root cause: `_convert` resolved `_pandoc_timeout()` per unit; `load_config()` performed root discovery before its result-cache lookup.\nProof: old 884-unit trace = 1,770 Popen calls (884 Pandoc + 886 git-root), 29.2378s. Repaired trace = 887 Popen calls (884 Pandoc + 3 cold root probes), 29.0194s. Exact bytes matched; all 884 Pandoc calls remained. This confirmed the lookup mechanism but measured only 0.2184s quiet-host savings, so it is not a material wall-clock RCA.\nTest: held-out three-unit resolution-count oracle was RED at 3 resolutions, GREEN at 1, exact defect seed returned RED at 4, then GREEN after restoration. Focused renderer suite: 90 passed.\nFix: sample timeout once per render pass and thread it through optional private-helper parameters; direct callers retain safe defaults.\nScope/safety: sole production caller and direct test callers were swept; no caller depends on lookup count. No new dependency, no assertion/test removal, no byte/fallback/timeout/reap behavior change.\nSiblings: no other production caller or parallel surface was missing the invariant.\nResidual risk: accepted — real Pandoc corpus work remains expensive by explicit ADR 0095 coverage contract; tracked by the CI-runtime umbrella for separate evidence-based remediation.\nReplication: Gerrit Verify run 31791259529 passed in 33m43s; LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, zero unresolved comments. macOS default suite was 26m39s and still performed every assertion.\nOSS comparison: Django LazySettings, Black configuration/mode passing, and pytest session-scoped Config all resolve loop/session invariants once (3/3 consensus). Back-out: Gerrit revert of 1773.","timestamp":1786704469907363001}],"created_at":1786684024685021001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"285a3892-360b-4ec6-a04b-199732a7ec1c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"cc7f-4a24-bc7a-4511"},{"link_uuid":"dbfd2c0b-19a4-48a2-95bb-4f3d44bb4e6c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ae78-c3ca-150f-42ec"}],"description":"## Context\nThe 884-unit hardening oracle invokes production `_convert` once per unit. `_convert` currently resolves `reconciler.dc_pandoc_timeout_s` on every invocation. A runtime trace on current origin/main d05bf2bc1be observed 100 Pandoc plus 102 `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` subprocesses for 100 conversions; resolving once at the render-pass boundary preserved identical outputs and reduced the trace to 100 Pandoc plus 3 one-time root probes. The prior 884-unit trace observed 1,770 total Popen calls (884 Pandoc + 886 root discovery). This is separate from the copied legacy oracle removed by absolute-diplomatic-snowyowl.\n\n## Contract and prior disposition\n- Preserve all real Pandoc calls, corpus units, byte expectations, timeout configurability, per-unit fallback, timeout, and process-group reap behavior.\n- absolute-diplomatic-snowyowl approved immutable outputs only for the copied legacy side and retained all 884 real production conversions. harmless-wavy-osprey approved session-scoped sharing that reduced duplicate work, while coercive-paediatric-bug rejected parallelism that does not reduce aggregate runner usage. No tracker ticket rejects render-pass configuration injection.\n- Full replacement of product Pandoc calls remains out of scope because ADR 0095 requires the real pinned boundary in every conversion assertion.\n\n## OSS consensus research (2026-08-14)\nAll three surveyed projects are active, unarchived, and popular: Django (88,426 stars; pushed 2026-08-13) lazily resolves each setting and caches it in `LazySettings.__dict__`; Black (41,804 stars; pushed 2026-08-10) reads pyproject configuration at CLI setup and passes resolved `mode` into multi-file workers; pytest (14,416 stars; pushed 2026-08-12) exposes its resolved Config as a session-scoped `pytestconfig` fixture. Consensus is 3/3 for resolving loop/session invariants once and passing them to repeated work.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add a held-out behavioral oracle with three proven renderable units and assert exactly one `_pandoc_timeout()` resolution for the whole render pass.\n2. Resolve timeout once in `render_markdown_to_wiki`; pass it through `_render_unit` and `_convert` using optional parameters so direct two-argument callers retain safe default behavior. The direct `_render_unit` caller at test_wiki_render_corpus.py:325 remains valid.\n3. Update the two `_convert` monkeypatch stand-ins at test_wiki_render.py:268/278 to accept the optional argument supplied by the public render path.\n4. In the 884-unit direct hardening loop, resolve timeout once outside the loop and pass it to `_convert`; keep exact expected bytes and all 884 real Pandoc invocations.\n5. Run held-out RED -> fixer -> GREEN, defect-seeded RED, focused hardening/corpus tests, lint, typecheck, and paired subprocess/timing measurement. The fresh-process measurement must observe 884 Pandoc launches, exactly one timeout resolution, and at most 3 one-time Git-root probes.\n6. Push through Gerrit; merge only after LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, no unresolved comments, then record CI and runner savings. Back-out is a Gerrit revert restoring per-call timeout resolution.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A render pass with three renderable units calls `_pandoc_timeout()` exactly once.\n- [ ] The hardening oracle launches all 884 real production Pandoc conversions.\n- [ ] A fresh 884-unit trace launches at most 3 `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` probes.\n- [ ] Non-default timeout configuration remains observable between separate render passes.\n- [ ] Per-unit timeout fallback behavior remains covered.\n- [ ] Pandoc stdin and argv behavior remains covered.\n- [ ] Byte-equivalence to all 884 immutable expected outputs remains covered.\n- [ ] Whole-process-group reap behavior remains covered.\n- [ ] Held-out RED/GREEN and exact defect-seeded RED are recorded.\n- [ ] Before/after subprocess counts and wall time quantify savings without claiming more than the evidence.\n- [ ] Focused tests, lint, and typecheck pass.\n- [ ] LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 pass before merge.\n- [ ] Final report cites OSS sources and prior-ticket dispositions.","env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py","reason":"Resolve the configured Pandoc timeout once per render pass and thread the value through backward-compatible private conversion helpers."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py","reason":"Add the behavioral resolution-count oracle and hoist timeout resolution outside the immutable 884-unit real-Pandoc loop."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py","reason":"Keep two existing _convert monkeypatch stand-ins compatible with the optional timeout argument supplied by the render path."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","managed_refs":[["relates_to","ae78-c3ca-150f-42ec"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"44480b26-a333-4ac3-a7cb-d1c073e8bfc2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["ci","performance","ubuntu","pandoc"],"ticket_id":"2364-663e-859d-4b58","ticket_type":"task","title":"Eliminate per-unit git root discovery from Pandoc conversion","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7425cbd3-f0c8-4000-a876-f8e2d6bd7382","2daf4a4c-23aa-49b6-ba1a-a8e43b59c350","13d0434e-4bca-40a0-be1d-1e646477aa25","df9ad132-e9e0-4d4d-baea-c495da381db3","945501c6-5c01-4e5e-9b68-a6fc56933fc4","65be2cf6-56f0-4d1a-87c3-35f5f1a4eecf","2523b73a-e66c-465b-a890-45a36608ac88","b9595103-fc1a-4a8f-b63f-4bfe20c6a48e","c8666a4b-9baa-4d34-8059-b34beacab5f2","dbfd2c0b-19a4-48a2-95bb-4f3d44bb4e6c","63ce2d0b-dd43-44a6-b8a0-1147d780c60e","44480b26-a333-4ac3-a7cb-d1c073e8bfc2"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786709651551164580,"uuid":"347bb290-3f46-4e06-a305-56455b954bf3"}